# Ensure Domain Model Usage on Code

## Domain Specification Location

The domain specification MUST reside in [`docs/domain-specification.md`](../../docs/domain-specification.md).  
It MUST contain **"Ubiquitous Language"**. Also follow [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Pre-Change Checklist (Before Any Code Change)

1. **Read** the domain specification (especially Ubiquitous Language).
2. **Question the change against the domain** — new entities, sync rules, YouTube fields, API labels?
3. Update the specification **first** if the domain changes.

**Do NOT write code or tests until answered.**

## Coding Rules

Identifiers MUST use domain terms: **Channel**, **Video**, **Comment**, **Sync**, **YouTube channel id** — not `ChannelData`, `fetchItems`, `ytObj`.

See [engage-tell-dont-ask.mdc](engage-tell-dont-ask.mdc), [engage-law-of-demeter.mdc](engage-law-of-demeter.mdc).

## Testing Rules

When tests exist, use domain scenario names (`shouldRegisterChannelWithYoutubeId`, `shouldListCommentsForVideo`).

## Post-Change Update Rule

Update `docs/domain-specification.md` and [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md) when concepts, routes, sync behavior, or invariants change.

## Violation Handling

Refactor technical names to domain terms when touching violating code.
